==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|natural|ist}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete|except as merged with later senses}} A [[natural philosopher]]; a [[scientist]]. {{defdate|16th–19th c.}}
#* {{RQ:Wollstonecraft Vindication Women|passage=It has also been asserted, by some '''naturalists''', that men do not attain their full growth and strength till thirty; but that women arrive at maturity by twenty.}}
# {{lb|en|philosophy}} A person who [[believe|believes]] in or [[advocate|advocates]] the tenets of [[philosophical]] or [[methodological]] [[naturalism]]. {{defdate|from 16th c.}}
# An expert in [[natural history]] or the study of [[plant]]s and [[animal]]s. {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Easy Phraseology for the Use of Those Persons Who Intend to Learn the Colloquial Part of the Italian Language|passage=I will leave off all my childish fooleries and diversions, and set about studying with such a rage, that when you come back next year, you may find the tongue I have now in my mouth more forky than that of some serpents mentioned by Pliny the '''naturalist'''.|year={{ante|1776}}|author=Joseph Baretti|page=236|authorlink=Giuseppe Marc'Antonio Baretti|chapter=Dialogue the Fortieth|publisher=Joseph Bocca|location=Turin|edition=1835|url=https://www.google.com.au/books/edition/Easy_Phraseology_for_the_Use_of_Those_Pe/nlEVAAAAYAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=0}}
# {{lb|en|art}} A creative [[artist]] who attempts to faithfully represent [[nature]]; an adherent of artistic [[naturalism]]. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}

